      "writtenOn": "2023-01-26T14:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Individual components of (VM) boot can and should check that hash_algorithms are the suitable ones - these are best suited to be small tests/unit tests.\n\nThis test in this patch is part of compatibility test suite and they validate devices against the Android CDD. These extend to partners who may not be running the unit tests mentioned above. In fact, I don\u0027t believe we even mandate pvmfw (yet?) \u0026 only use it as a reference. But Android does care deeply about Device Integrity \u0026 mandates verified boot to use `verification algorithms as strong as current recommendations from NIST for hashing algorithms (SHA-256)`. Since Virtualization extends verified boot, we need to ensure \u0027Android\u0027 devices follow these too.",
      "parentUuid": "f854c145_de5c2228",
      "range": {
